From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Settings top level in BlackBerry 10 order

Owner pick 2026-11-05 (reorder only): the Settings homepage keeps every
row but lists them in BlackBerry 10 style order.

* Sable comes first, in its own untitled group.
* Networks and connected devices, then Notifications, Sound and Modes,
  then Apps, Display, Wallpaper and Keyboard.
* Security and privacy moves above the device rows, and Accessibility
  joins it after Emergency.
* System, Storage, Battery and About close the list, in that order.

Nothing is hidden and search is unchanged. Both the classic and the
expressive homepage layouts get the same order.
